// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 13-expression-semantics
// facility: [Resolve-Unbound] (a built-in operation is only called); conf.builtin-name-as-value
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.unbound-name (static)
//
// `sizeof` names a built-in operation, which is called (`sizeof<T>()`) and
// has no value: as an index it is rejected before the program runs (it had
// reached `coby`'s evaluator, as an unbound name, and `cobc`'s code
// generator, as an internal error).

import std;

fn main()
{
    array<u64, 2> a = [1, 2];
    printf("%v\n", a[sizeof]);
}
